hey everyone welcome to yessi tv where  you can find weekly videos on minimalism  and healthy living to help you live a  simpler happier life  today i'm going to share with you seven  life lessons that i've learned from  working with dying patients  i used to be an icu nurse did that for a  few years  and then i completely changed gears to  hospice nursing  where i now help dying patients live  their best life  for whatever time they have left during  these years i've learned so much about  life  and for me personally number one truly  is the most valuable  time our time is limited i used to take  this sound for granted  i've wasted countless hours doing  useless things that did nothing to  better myself  or anyone else's lives i've seen  children die and i've seen  adults die unexpectedly children  especially hit me hard because i am a  mother  but it teaches me that we should never  take life for granted  not my own not my loved ones and don't  get me wrong it's not about the quantity  of time that you have  but for me knowing that my time is going  to run out  that i could die tomorrow changes the  way that i live  today my time your time it's running out  that's a fact  so two main questions i want you to ask  yourself are  number one what do i want to accomplish  before i die  and number two what kind of impact do i  want to have on other people's lives  before this happens whether you like it  or not you're going to leave a legacy  behind  so what's it going to be you get to  decide  lesson number two live with purpose when  people often talk about finding their  purpose in life they talk about  finding your passion pursue your passion  but passion isn't something that you're  just  born with and that's it it's something  that molds with you that develops  as you have new experiences meet new  people and try new things  i didn't have a passion for icu nursing  actually  quite the opposite but that experience  led me to  this job that i currently do feel very  passionately about  so learn and try new things i've come to  realize that  even as insignificant as my life might  be in the grand scheme of life  i have the ability to create change i  have the option of either shutting  myself  out and keeping myself boxed up in my  own little world  or offering a service to others and  making a difference  so the lesson here is live life  purposefully and the passion will come  to you  lesson number three might be a hard one  for some of you  who have lost a loved one and it is  letting go  can be an act of love i know some of you  might look at me like  what but letting go can be one of the  most loving things you can do  when i worked in icu i specifically  remember one older gentleman  who had suffered a long battle with  cancer he was ready to go  he was at peace with it and he actually  wanted to stop  all kinds of treatments his family they  had other ideas they wanted him to  continue  everything and he didn't want that when  they finally accepted his wishes  and it was time for him to go all of his  family was around his bedside  they shared stories they laughed they  cried together  they shared pictures they combed his  hair they made him  look nice and presentable he felt good  he smiled  when it finally came time for his death  one of his  daughters looked at me and said how can  you do this for a living this is so  sad i smiled warmly and said  no this is beautiful  you are all surrounding him with love  and you're giving him  a dignified death that he would have  wanted  when a family member chooses to let  someone go naturally  instead of hanging on for their own good  and for their own benefits  that is love lesson number four is on  humility we are so fragile and whether  you're rich poor  white black or brown you will not escape  death  so we should always be humble some of my  patients live in million dollar homes  with gorgeous chandeliers  intricate furniture and acres and acres  of land  but they don't have the health to enjoy  it now don't get me wrong i don't think  it's bad to pursue wealth if you want to  make a positive impact in the world  but know that wealth comes from within  the rich man is not he who has the most  but he who needs the least  i had a very wealthy mom want to sue the  hospital because we couldn't fix her  son's  weakened heart from years of nephews  unfortunately  her money or her power was not going to  save him  i also had a racist patient had to deal  with the fact that a mexican nurse  gave him cpr and saved his life the  irony  right we are all human and we deserve  the same dignity and respect  so let's be humble lesson number five  love  every single day  this one happened almost three years ago  and it still sometimes makes me cry  a mom lying in the hospital bed with her  child  holding him tightly and caressing his  head as he took his last breath  we could not save him i don't know if  your family is broken or if you're as  happy as can be but there is  always someone in your life that you can  give love to  it can be as simple as giving an  encouraging word or helping that older  adult  carry your groceries into the car when  you give love  your brain perceives love it makes you  happier  but not only that it gives you a sense  of purpose and by focusing on  serving and loving others it can  definitely give you a greater sense of  accomplishment  for my husband and i there's not a day  that we don't tell each other by before  going to work because we don't know if  we'll be back my challenge to you is  think of  one simple thing that you can do every  day to give love to the people in your  life  it can be as simple as calling a friend  or reading a bedtime story with your  child every night  and for greater accountability let me  know in the comments what your act of  love is going to be  but keep it pg lesson number six  the bucket list i had a patient just  last week  actually a two-year-old whose battle  with brain cancer has been extremely  rough  for both her and her family and her  parents really wanted to give her the  experience of being able to go to the  beach  at least once in her life they had to  plan meticulously between tube feedings  medications  and making sure that she didn't stick  anything in her mouth because she's  immunocompromised  it was quite an ordeal for them to plan  this out and to do it safely  but the thing is they did it this little  girl got to go to the beach she got to  stick her little toesies in the sand and  feel an ocean breeze  for what might have been her last time  what is your bucket list  that thing that you've always wanted to  do that you've been putting off  i'm not saying go crazy and go bankrupt  on expensive and frivolous vacations  but enjoy and explore the world around  you make  it count lesson number seven is on fear  of failure  in my interview with entrepreneur tammy  williams  she mentions that to conquer her fear of  failure she had to acknowledge that so  long as something  isn't dead she can fix whatever she's  failed in when my husband and i started  our company  we lost 16 thousand dollars it  hurt i cried a lot because that meant  months of free labor  down the drain but you know what money  truly does come and go and i now have  learned  that failure is not something to fear  but actually something to pursue  okay surely you're thinking she's nuts i  love the saying  those who have never failed have never  tried  if there is something that you're unsure  of doing or trying  because you're afraid of failure then  ask yourself this question  if i were dying would i regret not  having tried  okay guys i could probably go on for  hours talking about the topic of death  and dying because i'm truly passionate  about giving people their best life  for whatever time they have left but i  don't want to put you to sleep  so for sticking to the end i just want  to give you one last piece of advice  be present even if you're bored and have  nothing to do  then enjoy the air that you're breathing  in because some people have pain with  every breath they take enjoy the way the  birds sing because some people can't  hear them  enjoy the way the breeze makes a leaf  move on a tree  because some people can't see it so  whatever you're doing and whoever you're  doing it with  actually be present and in the moment  that's it for today guys  if you like this video please give it a  thumbs up and subscribe so you won't  miss out on my weekly videos  i thank you so so much for watching this  video because it's truly very special to  me  and i hope to see you in the next one
 

